Subject: [PATCH 20/21] context: retain due timers when a context lock is busy

A deferred timer must remain discoverable by the next scheduler scan.
The actual source excerpt fails the contention regression before this patch
and passes all three host checks after it. No kernel/IRQ/guest proof claimed.

Agent: Codex
Model: gpt-6-sol
Provider: OpenAI
Refs: wy-1792956367-diag; wy-kernel-wake-root-red/green-20261025T1955
---
 src/context/switch.rs | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/context/switch.rs b/src/context/switch.rs
index 863ee7fc..6e570c28 100644
--- a/src/context/switch.rs
+++ b/src/context/switch.rs
@@ -332,6 +332,13 @@ fn schedule(
             }
         });
 
+        // Retry contended due entries on a later scan instead of clearing them
+        // with the temporary buffer at the start of the next scan.
+        if !timers.is_empty() {
+            let mut run_queue = percpu.switch_internals.run_queue.lock();
+            run_queue.timers.extend(timers.drain(..));
+        }
+
         // Drain from percpu
         {
             let mut local_wake = percpu.switch_internals.local_wakeup_list.borrow_mut();
